      "template_note": "Traffic damper optimization template for the in-process OpenSeesPy solver. Single objective: girder-end cumulative displacement. The load case path, dt, duration and per-node traffic_load_mappings are supplied only by the approval-frozen load Artifact pair (dense 163-column force matrix plus its node/column mapping); this template ships no bundled traffic record and no node list on purpose. traffic_load_mappings is written by the dispatcher with one entry per node, each carrying its own source_column and scale=1.0, because traffic is a moving load: every node owns an independent time history and the OpenSees traffic module would otherwise fall back to applying the whole matrix column at every node. response_nodes is narrowed to node 1 alone because the opensees-csv postprocessor has no cumulative_displacement_node selector: its displacement column is a step-wise max-abs envelope over response_nodes, so keeping node 72 here would silently redefine the objective the ANSYS side pins to node 1. Shear and moment are deliberately NOT optimization objectives."
    }
  },
